{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Incline</b> [your ear], <b>that</b> [they may be], <b>to be</b>, <b>have I not</b>, <b>to make known to you</b> — [verses] 17–21: five joined [words]." "<b>For my knowledge is pleasant</b> — to learn knowledge, for [it is] pleasant, my knowledge. Or, for it will be pleasant when you keep them. <b>In your belly</b>: an allusion to the heart."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:12.948078248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}